{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1446929-dragon-blooded-charm-rework-homebrew-wip","id":1446929,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm Rework Homebrew [WIP]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-02T01:43:57-07:00","id":1446929,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Charm Rework Homebrew [WIP]","content":"<div align=\"center\">Earth!<br /> Wind!<br /> Fire!<br /> Water!<br /> <s>Heart!</s> Wood!<br /> <br /> Go Dragons!</div><br /> The Dragon-Blooded are Chosen of the Five Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> Their power comes from their blood.<br /> <br /> They control the five elements of Creation.<br /> <br /> Why are they Ability Exalts again?<br /> <br /> Solars are Ability Exalts. They don't draw their power from an inherited mystical connection to the elements. They're normal people Chosen by the Sun who express their power through supernatural skill.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are Ability Exalts. They're the dark mirrors of the genius Solars, corrupted with the power of death.<br /> <br /> Lunars are Attribute Exalts. They're defined by their raw potential.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are Attribute Exalts. They're built. Their powers are built into their bodies.<br /> <br /> This makes at least a certain kind of sense. It's fiction about magical demigods, but I can follow the logic.<br /> <br /> But tying Dragon-Blooded powers, which are literally the result of their breeding, to their skill in trained abilities... I don't follow.<br /> <br /> &quot;Because I say so!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sorry, doesn't cut it.<br /> <br /> I propose reworking the DB charmset around the Five Elements. Much like how 2E Infernals were based around the Yozi.<br /> <br /> I haven't actually got a solid idea to show off yet. But I did something similar in 2E to make it easier to run NPCs and I'll be stealing liberally from <i>Terrene</i>, but here's the basic principles:<br /> <br /> Five groupings of Charms: Air, Earth, Fire, Water, and Wood.<br /> No Charms that add charm dice; just successes<br /> A Charm Success Cap of 3: DBs can add no more than three auto successes to their rolls from magic, charm dice count as half a success<br /> DBs get an omni-applicable Excellency for free that allows them to add upto three successes on any roll for 2m each.*<br /> A limited number of dice tricks -- Double X, Reroll X, X Explodes, +X non-Charm dice are all powerful effects but they're boring. Charms should do something. &quot;This Charm does Y and <i>also</i> gives double-9s&quot; is a good Charm. &quot;This Charm gives double-9s&quot; is kinda &quot;meh&quot;.<br /> Keeping the idea of the Aura mechanic, though changing the execution<br /> Whilst we're here, this isn't trying to rewrite 3E. I don't like &quot;Duration: Scene&quot;. I would much prefer something like &quot;Duration: One Hour&quot;. But that's not how 3E works. I'm rewriting Dragon-Blooded Charms, not how the game works.<br /> <br /> *Might scrap that for how Power works in Terrene: you can buy one success for 1m or three successes for 1m 1a<br /> <br /> The goal here would be to make each element support any concept but through the lens of an elemental archetype.<br /> <br /> A Fire Swordfighter might rely on speed and setting folks on fire. An Air Swordfighter might rely on accuracy and freezing folks. An Earth Swordfighter is using powerful blows that hit like a boulder. The Water fighter is fluid and graceful. The Wood fighter has a poison and is filled themselves with vitality. But they're all viable, equally capable, combat characters. And you can replace &quot;swordfighter&quot; with &quot;archer&quot; or &quot;brawler&quot; or any other combat style.<br /> <br /> So why the thread?<br /> <br /> Well, I'd like to gauge what other people want from DBs. What do you like about the official charms? What would you want from a charm rework?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T02:28:32-07:00","id":1446931,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure someone already floated this idea on a different forum back in the 2E era. I thought it was neat even back then. Go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T02:37:04-07:00","id":1446932,"title":"","content":"I would love something like this. It would help them be distinct and not solar-but-worse. <br /> <br /> Having dice tricks are only boring if the design for them are boring. Giving the Fire Melee charm a double 10s on decisive damage while fighting in a burning building, near lava or charging through a bonfire is not. It gives inspiration for stunts and if kept simple (same or similar circumstances for all fire combat charms for example) keeps things simple enough. Also helps with strategies and tactics for playstyles. Not to mention for a player group makes it obvious when a certain player has their time to shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13615-slovorg","name":"slovorg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T05:23:42-07:00","id":1446957,"title":"","content":"I think having 5 Element-based charmtrees is an excellent space for Dragon-Blooded to occupy. I'm reminded somewhat of A Clutch of Dragons, the 3e Deebs-before-Deebs, where each Ability was written with a separate tree for each element. Most Abilities only covered three Elements, but some like War and Melee had trees for all five. I think that this was a neat design choice, because it felt like it sort of sculpted the Charmtree based on the themes of each element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T06:24:55-07:00","id":1446963,"title":"","content":"Well, the Word-Of-Morke (YMMV on that) version is of why Ability Charms for Exalted, not specifically Dragon-blooded, was (paraphrasing from perhaps faulty memory) &quot;Because all the Exalted are heroic in human terms in the sense of doing feats of legend, which are versions of the normal deeds done by humans, empowered by Essence&quot;. And to that end, all their Charms are 'hooked' to one of the two things people in Exalted roll to do deeds; an Ability or an Attribute. It's a game about epic heroes who do heroic deeds of legend (as opposed to something like different types of magicians).<br /> <br /> (This is kind of what 'Classical' Charms are, in the main, supposed to do; even if you're conjuring up something from Essence in golden light, it's a tool to help you with an action, or if they're transforming you, its into a bigger and stronger Beastman form where you still fight like a human person, or at most extreme its a Sidereal spell-like effect which nonetheless has a clear primary goal in helping you with the purpose of the ability, like solving an investigation, or getting you somewhere fast, or helping a ship fast travel, and so on.)<br /> <br /> (I'd say there are some potential problems in this of course particularly in 3e in that the 'new Exalts' seem to collide directly with this creative agenda in the opposite direction! But then since they're still optional vaporware, it's not necessarily a huge issue.)<br /> <br /> You can definitely unmoor Charms complete from Ability+Attribute, but I would say for me it's not as interesting as doing what Exalted in this sense does that other fantasy games don't do (and which feels fairly integral to me in how its blending chi-based martial arts heroes and epic deed Sword and Sorcery heroes), while if I wanted strong heroes who didn't have 'heroic action' based Charms, I'd look to go to uncapping God-blooded power levels or something like this.<br /> <br /> Apologies if this is not an immediately useful response to your proposal, I thought it might be useful to least hash out and articulate that bit though, and then hopefully with that out of the way the thread can then get on with some more productive dialogue between you and people who accept the basic premise of your rework and have proper constructive suggestions to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T08:18:24-07:00","id":1446982,"title":"","content":"In regards to &quot;why ability not attibute&quot;, The distinction seems to be that ability exalts have mostly externally-focused charms, while attribute exalts have internally-focused charms. <br /> <br /> Solars affect the world around them with their skills, dragon blooded manipulate the world's elements. External.<br /> <br /> Lunars transform their bodies until it's the perfect tool for the job, Liminals incorporate the parts they need taken from elsewhere. Internal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T08:35:32-07:00","id":1446986,"title":"","content":"I think that maybe having an omni applicable excellency and an unconditional charm dice cap might be a bit too wide. What if each element had three excellencies, and each one raised the cap on it by 1 success, but they\u2019d also have to do something in addition to raising the cap. I was thinking each one upgrading the scope that you can use your elemental trick anima power, but to stop it from getting out of hand you might need to raise the cost of the trick if you\u2019re using it for larger scope things. You can\u2019t just use one mote to seal off a cavern passage with earth, even if you have all three Earth excellencies.<br /> <br /> I definitely like the idea of keeping the aura mechanic though. Soak boosting charms are pretty clearly Earth/Wood mainly, unless you\u2019re boosting soak against environmental fire damage or something, so I\u2019d like incentive for my non-earth characters not to always end up with stone skin. A DB that fights with a flaming blade and preorders them self with stone skin is cool, but I don\u2019t want it to be strictly better than the guy just using fire.<br /> <br /> Also to that end maybe leave some intentional holes. Like the earth aspect doesn\u2019t get a defence pentathlon negator, but instead adds soak/hardness equal to their current penalty or something. <br /> <br /> Otherwise I think it should be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T10:15:27-07:00","id":1446995,"title":"","content":"I would personally focus on teamwork. Something dragon-blooded should have had in all their charmset but is only prevalent in the War charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}